From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 10:19:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] phosh-session: Device updates of phoc.ini reach a user with
 saved modes

Plinius: once mode or scale were applied in Settings, phosh-session
started phoc with the user's copy of the system phoc.ini (0009), and
whatever a device update changed in the system file later never reached
phoc: here the light sensor's box (phoc-plinius 0034).

phoc now starts with $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/phoc.ini: the system file as it is
now, with only mode and scale of each output from the user's copy
(phoc-ini-merge, packaged with phosh-plinius). If that fails the copy is
used as before.
---
 data/phosh-session.in | 17 ++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/data/phosh-session.in b/data/phosh-session.in
index abf35912..3bbf55d2 100755
--- a/data/phosh-session.in
+++ b/data/phosh-session.in
@@ -40,9 +40,20 @@ if [ -f /etc/phosh/phoc.ini ]; then
   PHOC_INI=/etc/phosh/phoc.ini
 fi
 
-# Mode and scale picked in Settings, saved by phosh on top of the system phoc.ini
-if [ -f "${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/phosh/phoc.ini" ]; then
-  PHOC_INI="${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/phosh/phoc.ini"
+# Mode and scale picked in Settings, saved by phosh with a copy of the system phoc.ini. phoc
+# starts with the system file as it is now plus mode and scale from that copy: a device update
+# of the system file reaches it too. The copy as it is only if that fails.
+USER_PHOC_INI="${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/phosh/phoc.ini"
+MERGED_PHOC_INI="$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/phoc.ini"
+if [ -f "$USER_PHOC_INI" ]; then
+  if [ -d "$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR" ] &&
+     @libexecdir@/plinius/phoc-ini-merge "$PHOC_INI" "$USER_PHOC_INI" > "$MERGED_PHOC_INI.new" &&
+     mv -f "$MERGED_PHOC_INI.new" "$MERGED_PHOC_INI"; then
+    PHOC_INI="$MERGED_PHOC_INI"
+  else
+    [ -d "$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR" ] && rm -f "$MERGED_PHOC_INI.new"
+    PHOC_INI="$USER_PHOC_INI"
+  fi
 fi
 
 if [ -f "$HOME/.phoshdebug" ]; then
